  "description": "Virginia's 4th Congressional District covers the city of Richmond and portions of Southside Virginia along Interstate 95, including Colonial Heights, Emporia, Hopewell, and Petersburg. The incumbent is Democrat Jennifer McClellan, first elected in a 2023 special election and re-elected in 2024 with 67.3% of the vote. The district is rated Solid Democratic by Cook Political Report, Inside Elections, and Sabato's Crystal Ball, making it a safe seat for the incumbent. No Republican candidate filed by the May 25 primary deadline, though the party may nominate a candidate by August 4; two independent candidates — Jason Brown II and Andre Kersey — are running in the general election.",
